  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14244490/assets/fc0ad365fca91e61da2e7f09197299ea6130018d7490873d3568231be360b481.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the graph of $y=\\frac{a}{x}.$ What is the value of $a?$",
  "worked_solution": "Notice that the point $(3,-1)$ lies on the graph.\n\nSubstituting its coordinates into the equation $y=\\frac{a}{x},$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1=\\frac{a}{3}\\,⟹\\,a=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
